To convert Markdown to HTML in C++, you can use an external library like `markdown` or `libsoup`. These libraries handle the conversion for you. Below is an example using the `markdown` library, which is widely used and well-maintained.

First, you need to install the `markdown` library. On Ubuntu, you can install it via:

```sh
sudo apt-get install libmarkdown-dev
```

Then, you can create a simple C++ function to perform the conversion:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <libmarkdown/libmarkdown.h>
#include <libmarkdown/html.h>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdownText) {
    // Initialize the markdown parser
    struct md_parser* parser = md_parse_new();

    // Parse the markdown text
    struct md_document* document = md_parse(parser, markdownText.c_str(), markdownText.size());

    // Convert the parsed markdown to HTML
    char* html = md_document_to_html(document);

    // Get the HTML string
    std::string htmlString(html);

    // Free the allocated resources
    free(html);
    md_document_free(document);
    md_parse_free(parser);

    return htmlString;
}

